        "original_id": "70ec509c-2968-5fd7-9cf8-0d13c146d007",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Charles Fraser-Smith, Ian Fleming, Q\n- Fictional Roles and Systems: James Bond quartermaster, Q Branch, Q Division, British Secret Service\n- Works and Franchises: James Bond films, film novelisations\n\nFacts:\n- Charles Fraser-Smith was born on 26 January 1904 and died on 9 November 1992.\n- Charles Fraser-Smith was an author and a one-time missionary.\n- Charles Fraser-Smith is widely credited as the inspiration for Ian Fleming's James Bond quartermaster Q.\n- Q is a fictional character in the James Bond films and film novelisations.\n- Q is the head of Q Branch, later called Q Division, which is the fictional research and development division of the British Secret Service.",
